# Canonical Hazync guest image id (METHOD_ID).
#
# `docker build -f reproduce/Dockerfile .` produces EXACTLY this id on any machine (the container runs
# provision-vps.sh as root at fixed /root paths with the pinned toolchain). Verifiers check proofs
# against this id; a host that yields a different id was NOT built from the canonical guest and will
# not verify the published proofs — see docs/PROVING.md.
#
# Inputs (all pinned): Bitcoin Core v28.0, secp256k1 v0.5.1, rzup rust 1.94.1 / cpp 2024.1.5 /
# cargo-risczero 3.0.5 / r0vm 3.0.5, risc0 crates =3.0.5, committed Cargo.lock, built at fixed paths.
#
# ⚠ ANY EDIT TO GUEST SOURCE THAT MOVES LINE NUMBERS CHANGES THIS ID — INCLUDING COMMENTS.
#
# ⚠ AND "GUEST SOURCE" IS WIDER THAN prover/methods/guest/. The guest #[path]-INCLUDES source from
# elsewhere in the tree, and it compiles into the ELF like any other guest code:
#
#     coinbase-smt/src/roots.rs   — the roots-only half of the BIP30 coinbase SMT (hazync#54)
#     coinbase-smt/src/bip30.rs   — the per-block BIP30 state transition
#
# These are #[path] INCLUDES, not Cargo path dependencies, and the distinction is the whole of hazync#88:
# Cargo makes a path dependency ABSOLUTE, Rust embeds it in panic metadata, and the id then depends on
# where the repo happens to be checked out. Including the file keeps ONE copy (no drift between the
# guest's check and the host's) while keeping the recorded path relative. Do not convert these back.
#
# A crate in that list can sit anywhere in the tree and have its own host-side test suite, and editing
# it is still a re-baseline. This is not hypothetical: adding a five-line `empty_root()` helper to
# coinbase-smt/src/lib.rs, for a host-side genesis pin, moved the id from 4ea6567b… to 35cfbbed…, with
# nothing under prover/methods/guest/ changed. scripts/check-guest-inputs.sh keeps this list honest and
# keeps a matching notice at the top of each such crate, where whoever is editing it will see it.
#
# Measured 2026-08-02, because the opposite was assumed: adding FIFTEEN LINES OF PURE COMMENT to
# prover/methods/guest/src/main.rs (no code, only `///` and `//`) moved the id from be5e0528… to
# 2a334ebe…. CI's reproducible-image-id job is what caught it.
#
# The mechanism is panic-location metadata: Rust embeds file and line into panic machinery, so
# inserting a line shifts every subsequent line number and the ELF changes with it.
#
# The practical consequence, which is easy to get wrong: a "harmless" comment or a reformat in
# prover/methods/guest/ is a RE-BASELINE. It invalidates every proof on the board just as surely as a
# consensus change would. Batch guest documentation into a change that is already re-baselining —
# never land it on its own, and never assume a docs-only guest diff is free.
