# WHAT CHANGED IN THE GUEST
#
# 1. BIP30 is now PROVEN, not argued (#54). The old check leaned on BIP34 making coinbase txids unique
#    per height, which is sound and EXPIRES at ~1,983,702 — the height where a BIP34 height-push can
#    reproduce a pre-BIP34 coinbase scriptSig. A second accumulator replaces it: a coinbase-only sparse
#    Merkle tree (txid -> unspent output count) whose root is journalled beside the utreexo roots and
#    enforced at the fold seam. Absence and a zero count are the same state, so "prove it is absent" is
#    exactly "prove BIP30 is satisfied", and a fully-spent duplicate stays legal — which it must, since
#    Core accepted one in 2010. The ceiling is gone: nothing in the check depends on scriptSig encoding.
#
# 2. Blocks 91842/91880 are grandfathered ON THE SMT PATH (audit #3 F-1). Their coinbases duplicated
#    earlier ones that were STILL UNSPENT — the entire reason BIP30 exists — so entering them the tree
#    holds the txid with a nonzero count and NO absence proof can exist. Without the exception the
#    check is reject-valid on real history and a from-genesis prover stalls at 91841, ~10% in. Gated on
#    the block hash in BOTH directions, exactly as the utreexo F3 overwrite is.
#
# 3. BIP34Height is read from Core instead of typed (#83 sweep). Its four siblings — BIP66, BIP65, CSV,
#    Segwit — were already read from Core's compiled Consensus::Params and asserted on every proving
#    path. 227931 was a literal in two places with nothing checking it, while this very file claimed
#    "nothing consensus-relevant is a hand-typed magic number now". Now true.
#
